      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Tender: RHS says not hardy in the UK, wait for nights above 10 C before putting it out, and it dislikes cold, damp conditions; the 10 C minimum is the agent's reading of that advice (the Penn State indoor-herbs page, read only as a model summary of a truncated page, says it cannot survive below 50 F, about the same). Usually treated as an annual. Watering: RHS evenly moist, hates wet roots overnight; NC State moist well-drained. Size: RHS 20 to 50 cm tall; spread taken from NC State (up to 1 ft 2 in); NC State's wider range is 4 in to 3 ft by cultivar. Toxicity: ASPCA lists basil as non-toxic to dogs and cats and NC State tags it the same."
